Making them that long seems to defeat the purpose, since notes should really
be represented with single syllables. Also, I believe the discussion was
meant to create a system that could be used as a language feature, so
quoting them wouldn't really work in that sense. Other than that, quoting
would work fine as far as I know, but I am no musician. Using the actual
letters would also not work for having notes represented by a  single
syllable (i.e., {.abu} and {.ebu}), so maybe a number system would be best?

